<title>VENEZUELA: Lufthansa to suspend Caracas, Quito flights.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa to suspend Caracas, Quito flights.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German airline Deutsche Lufthansa AG will suspend its thrice-weekly flights from Frankfurt to Caracas, Venezuela and from Frankfurt to Quito, Ecuador as of March 1997, Lufthansa said.</p>
<p>The company said the decision was the result of lower than expected returns on the two South American runs and forms part of a larger company restructuring and cost-cutting program that aims to reduce unit costs by 20 percent by 2001.</p>
<p>-- John Paul Rathbone, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
